ATTRIBUTION
-----------

Stable Diffusion on the Qualcomm Hexagon NPU
    xororz/local-dream
    https://github.com/xororz/local-dream
    Licensed CC BY-NC 4.0

    The C++ inference server in this project is a fork of local-dream's.
    The QNN pipelines, the model conversion process, the per chipset build
    tiers and the device capability gating are all that project's work.
    The Stable Diffusion checkpoint archives and the upscaler weights this
    app downloads are published by the same author.

    Modifications made here: the pipeline was decomposed into individually
    addressable ops (encode_text, sample, vae_encode, vae_decode,
    latent_blend) exposed over HTTP, with conditionings and latents held
    server side behind handles.

LocalDream
    https://github.com/AbrahamPaulJ/dreamui
    A consumer application built on the same backend.

    The mask editor's brush behaviour, its compositing rules, and the batch
    result strip are ported from it rather than reimplemented.


THIRD PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

Qualcomm AI Runtime (QAIRT / QNN)
    Qualcomm Technologies, Inc.
    Runtime libraries used to execute models on the Hexagon NPU. Distributed
    under Qualcomm's own licence terms, which are separate from and not
    superseded by this project's licence. Not included in this repository.

QuickJS
    Fabrice Bellard and Charlie Gordon
    https://bellard.org/quickjs/
    MIT licensed. Used as the sandbox for plugin nodes. Fetched at build
    time rather than vendored.

MNN
    Alibaba
    https://github.com/alibaba/MNN
    Apache 2.0. Used for CPU and GPU model execution paths.

Real-ESRGAN x4plus anime 6B, 4x UltraSharpV2 Lite
    Upscaler weights, converted and published by xororz.
    Downloaded by the app at the user's request; not included here.

Neodragon
    Qualcomm AI Research
    https://huggingface.co/Qualcomm-AI-Research/Neodragon
    BSD-3-Clause-Clear, with additional terms on the model card (the repo is
    tagged both "bsd-3-clause-clear" and "other" -- read it before
    redistributing the weights). The text to video model. The pipeline this app
    implements -- the pyramidal schedule, the autoregressive MMDiT loop and
    the streaming VAE decode -- follows their work; the NPU conversions it
    runs were made from their weights. Downloaded by the app at the user's
    request; not included here.

SSD-1B
    Segmind
    https://huggingface.co/segmind/SSD-1B
    Apache 2.0. Generates the first frame a video is animated from.

CLIP, DistilT5
    Text encoders used by the video path, converted for the NPU.
    Downloaded by the app at the user's request; not included here.

DiT engine (libdit_engine.so and its Hexagon skels)
    Built by xororz/local-dream (v3.0.0-alpha.1) from stable-diffusion.cpp
    with ggml's Hexagon backend, and shipped prebuilt inside this app. Runs
    FLUX.2 Klein and Z-Image Turbo on the NPU. Not included in this repository.

stable-diffusion.cpp
    leejet, with Hexagon optimisation by happyyzy
    https://github.com/happyyzy/stable-diffusion.cpp
    MIT licensed. Inside the DiT engine.

ggml
    ggml authors
    https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml
    MIT licensed. Inside the DiT engine.

FLUX.2 [klein] 4B
    Black Forest Labs
    https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4b-fp8
    Apache 2.0. Downloaded by the app at the user's request; not included here.

Z-Image Turbo
    Tongyi-MAI; fp8 weights by Kijai
    https://huggingface.co/Kijai/Z-Image_comfy_fp8_scaled
    Apache 2.0. Downloaded by the app at the user's request; not included here.

Qwen3-4B text encoder, DiT VAEs
    Converted for stable-diffusion.cpp by zhiyuanasad
    https://huggingface.co/zhiyuanasad/flux2_klein_adreno
    https://huggingface.co/zhiyuanasad/z_image_turbo_adreno
    Downloaded by the app at the user's request; not included here.


